## The question of “why”:
There are people who — for whatever reason (e.g., diabetes) — must or want to monitor their blood sugar very strictly.  
The idea behind this ice cream is to avoid digestible carbohydrates extremely strictly.  
The goal was to get below 10 g effective carbs per kg.  
(AI says/estimates that this recipe with unsweetened almond milk is at ~20–25 g effective carbohydrates per kg.)  
→ For comparison: supermarket ice cream is at 180–300 g/kg carbohydrates.

A second goal is to use only “good” additives.  
For example, carrageenan is controversial (suspected of being inflammation‑inducing) and is therefore deliberately not used in this recipe.  
Inulin, on the other hand, is good for gut flora.  
→ effectively an ingredient list that is better than conventional ice cream.

